theory.intro:
The **tangent** to $y=f(x)$ at $P(x_1, y_1)$ is the straight line that touches the curve there, with gradient $m = f'(x_1)$. The **normal** is the line through $P$ at right angles to the tangent. Find either equation from $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\draw[->] (-3.8,0) -- (3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.0) -- (0,2.6) node[above] {$y$};
\coordinate (P) at (1,-1);
\coordinate (Tm) at (-0.2,-2.2);
\coordinate (Tp) at (3.0,1.0);
\coordinate (Nu) at (-1.0,1.0);
\coordinate (Nd) at (2.6,-2.6);
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.2:2.6, smooth, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {0.5*\x*\x - 1.5}) node[pos=0.03, left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (Tm) -- (Tp) node[pos=0, below left] {tangent};
\draw[thick] (Nu) -- (Nd) node[pos=1, below left] {normal};
\coordinate (a) at ($(P)!0.3cm!(Tm)$);
\coordinate (b) at ($(P)!0.3cm!(Nd)$);
\draw (a) -- ($(a)+(b)-(P)$) -- (b);
\fill (P) circle (2pt);
\node[right=6pt] at (P) {$P(x_1,y_1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
Find the area of the right-angled triangle bounded by the coordinate axes and the tangent to $y = x^2 + 1$ at $(2, 5)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4.5) -- (0,7.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3} { \draw (\x,0.15) -- (\x,-0.15) node[below, font=\scriptsize] {$\x$};
}
\foreach \y in {-4,-2,2,4,6} { \draw (0.15,\y) -- (-0.15,\y) node[left, font=\scriptsize] {$\y$};
}
\node[below left, font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$O$};
\fill[gray!20] (0,0) -- (0.75,0) -- (0,-3) -- cycle;
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.0:2.35, smooth, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {\x*\x + 1});
\node[left] at (-1.3,2.69) {$y = x^2 + 1$};
\draw[thick] (-0.3,-4.2) -- (2.45,6.8);
\fill (2,5) circle (2.5pt);
\node[right=2pt] at (2,5) {$(2,5)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
The tangent to $y = 9 - x^2$ at the point $P(1, 8)$ intersects the $x$-axis at $A$ and the $y$-axis at $B$.
Find the area of $\triangle OAB$, where $O$ is the origin.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\draw[->] (-4.2,0) -- (6.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.6) -- (0,12.0) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,6} { \draw (\x,0.15) -- (\x,-0.15) node[below, font=\scriptsize] {$\x$};
}
\draw (5,0.15) -- (5,-0.15);
\node[above right=2pt] at (5,0) {$A$};
\foreach \y in {-2,2,4,6,8} { \draw (0.15,\y) -- (-0.15,\y) node[left, font=\scriptsize] {$\y$};
}
\draw (0.15,10) -- (-0.15,10);
\node[above left=3pt] at (0,10) {$B$};
\node[below left, font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$O$};
\fill[gray!20] (0,0) -- (5,0) -- (0,10) -- cycle;
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3.3:3.3, smooth, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {9 - \x*\x});
\node[left] at (-2.2,4.16) {$y = 9 - x^2$};
\draw[thick] (-0.6,11.2) -- (5.6,-1.2);
\fill (1,8) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right=2pt] at (1,8) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
